Hmm, but actually where is resolvePool called in loadContext vs action? reviewPoolLegSetup.reviewerPoolRoundSetup wraps in try/catch: "reviewer pool round setup failed (non-fatal, single-reviewer round):" — WAIT. It catches the error and logs a warning, returning null! So an unknown reviewer name in config does NOT fail the leg — it logs "(non-fatal)" and proceeds single-reviewer!

